      "card_ids": ["C14"],
      "claim": "In the fasted state, the absolute oral bioavailability of a 1500 mg GSK1322322 tablet was 57% in healthy volunteers, supporting high F for the query under fasted conditions.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "The query molecule (oxycodone) is a morphinan opioid with a 4,5-epoxy bridge, 6-keto, 14-hydroxy, and N-methyl groups. All related experimental evidence reports oral bioavailability values well above the 20% threshold, ranging from 25% to 98%. The most transferable analogues—tramadol (68%, opioid) and LSD (80%, rigid polycyclic alkaloid)—strongly support high oral bioavailability. No contradictory evidence exists. Therefore, the prediction is high.",
